      "title": "OpenAI: The Dawn of Generative Intelligence",
      "summary": "Tech leaders founded OpenAI in 2015 as a research lab committed to safe artificial intelligence. Leveraging the Transformer architecture, OpenAI scaled massive language models from GPT-1 to GPT-3. The launch of ChatGPT in late 2022 democratized generative AI, ushering in a technological revolution.",
      "content": "For decades, artificial intelligence research oscillated between bursts of optimism and prolonged 'AI winters.' Early systems relied on rigid rules and expert systems that struggled with the messy, unpredictable nuances of human language and visual perception.\n\nIn December 2015, a small group of prominent technologists—including Sam Altman, Greg Brockman, Elon Musk, and computer scientist Ilya Sutskever—gathered in San Francisco to establish OpenAI as a non-profit research institute. Their mission was to build safe artificial general intelligence (AGI) that would benefit all of humanity.\n\nWhile many researchers believed language comprehension required complex human-engineered grammar rules, OpenAI embraced a radical scaling hypothesis. They believed that neural networks, given vast computational clusters and immense quantities of text data, would learn to understand language organically.\n\nAdopting the revolutionary 'Transformer' neural network architecture introduced by Google researchers in 2017, OpenAI trained its Generative Pre-trained Transformer (GPT) models. Each generation grew by orders of magnitude: GPT-1, GPT-2, and GPT-3, which stunned researchers with its ability to compose poetry, debug computer software, and write persuasive prose.\n\nIn late November 2022, OpenAI released a research preview called ChatGPT, pairing its massive language model with a simple conversational interface and Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback (RLHF).\n\nThe reaction was unprecedented in the history of consumer software. Within five days, one million users logged on; within two months, ChatGPT reached one hundred million active users, becoming the fastest-growing consumer application in digital history.\n\nStudents, doctors, programmers, and artists used the conversational tool to summarize complex research, generate software code, and brainstorm creative projects. OpenAI transformed artificial intelligence from theoretical lab research into an omnipresent everyday assistant, inaugurating the generative AI era."
